    id: "econ-2021-hl-sa-q6-a", topicId: "economics-4-0", conceptId: "hdi-versus-gdp",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2021 HL Section A Q6(a)",
    questionText: "Explain why the Human Development Index (HDI) may provide a more accurate profile of human welfare in a country than the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) figure of that country.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"4 + 3","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 7,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "The HDI is a more accurate indicator of human welfare as it is a composite indicator which reflects the income per person, education and life expectancy of inhabitants of the country which impact on human welfare rather than simply considering the overall production level of the country. The HDI measure considers more variables which impact upon human welfare. GDP alone only reflects the level of economic activity within the country.", marks: 7, contextNote: "The scheme splits the 7 as 4 + 3: the HDI is a composite of income per person, education and life expectancy, where GDP reflects production alone.", openList: true },
    ],
