    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2025 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2025-hl-q14-b-ii-meaning", topicId: "economics-1-4", conceptId: "interpreting-a-ped-value",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2025 HL Q14(b)(ii) — economic meaning",
    stem: "Scentastic is a new deodorant. The PED is calculated from its market demand schedule.",
    questionText: "The price elasticity of demand (PED) for Scentastic, when its price rises from €2.00 to €2.50 and quantity demanded decreases from 30,000 units to 20,000 units, is −1.8. Explain the economic meaning of your answer.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"fixed","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 5,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "The sign is minus therefore Scentastic obeys the Law of Demand. There is an inverse relationship between the price and quantity demanded of Scentastic. The absolute value is 1.8. This demand for Scentastic is price elastic as its PED is greater than 1. The percentage change in the price of Scentastic will cause a greater percentage change in its quantity demanded. For every €1 increase in the price of Scentastic, its quantity demanded will decrease by 1.8%.", marks: 5, contextNote: "Both halves of the meaning: the minus sign, and the absolute value above 1.", openList: true },
    ],
